		"name": "Waai Media - User Management API",
		"description": "Comprehensive Postman Collection for the Waai Media Administrative User Management Module (Laravel 13 backend).\n\n### Overview:\nThe User Management module provides administration endpoints for listing, creating, inspecting, updating, changing roles, resetting passwords, and deleting user accounts.\n\n### Security & Business Constraints:\n1. **Admin Only**: All endpoints require a Bearer access token (`Authorization: Bearer <admin_token>`) belonging to an account with `role: admin` and the `access` ability.\n2. **Editor Forbidden**: Requests with an Editor token are rejected with `403 Forbidden`.\n3. **First Admin Protection**: The first admin ever created is permanently registered in `system_settings` and can never be deleted (`403 Forbidden`).\n4. **Last Active Admin Protection**: Demoting or deleting the last active admin is rejected with `403 Forbidden`.\n5. **Peer Admin Isolation**: An admin cannot update another admin's profile or reset another admin's password (`403 Forbidden`). Admins can update their own profile and editors' profiles.\n6. **Session Revocation**: Changing a user's role or resetting an editor's password automatically revokes all existing sessions/tokens for that user.\n\n### Variables:\n- `base_url`: Base API URL (e.g. `http://127.0.0.1:8000`).\n- `admin_token`: Sanctum access token for an Admin user.\n- `editor_token`: Sanctum access token for an Editor user (for negative testing).\n- `target_user_id`: ID of a user targeted for show, update, role change, password reset, or delete.",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
